// TEST: lie: a disguised 0+1+1+2 so(3) representation canonicalizes exactly onto the certifier's real-harmonic tables
// Lighthouse cell D4 (plan-latent-symmetry-learning.md §5 and §3.4 "canonicalization";
// RIGOR.md B4 (viii)). Input: J~_a = S D_a S^-1, the block-diagonal 0+1+1+2 tables D_a of
// MLLieDischarge.blockGenerator (d = 12) under a dense disguise S (cond 3.67), pasted from
// the dump-lie oracle (oracles/ml/Lie.fs `canonicalize`). Output: an orthogonal U with
// U J_a U^T = D_a. Every step is a theorem, not a fit:
// (0) E_i = a Frobenius-orthonormal basis of span{J~_a} (left singular vectors of the 144 x 3
//     vec stack); the Killing form kappa by lie.structure_constants / lie.killing.
// (i) Invariant metric. Omega = -2 sum_ij kinv_ij rhoW(E_i) rhoW(E_j), rhoW(E) S = -(E^T S + S E),
//     is the Casimir on bilinear forms: -L(L+1) on the spin-L forms of V (x) V (0 x6, -2 x39,
//     -6 x55, -12 x35, -20 x9). With -2 kinv = KQ diag(1/KLAM) KQ^T (eigh of -kappa/2) it is
//     sum_a rhoW(F_a)^2 over the (-kappa/2)-orthonormal frame F_a = sum_j KQ(j, a) E_j / sqrt(KLAM(a)):
//     Omega S = C^T S + S C + 2 sum_a F_a^T S F_a, C = sum_a F_a^2. Its spectral projector P0 onto
//     ker Omega (dim 6 = 1 + 4 + 1) along range Omega is the Haar average, so M = P0 vec(I) =
//     int g^T g dg is positive definite BY THEOREM. P0 is evaluated as the Riesz projector
//     lim (delta (Omega + delta I)^-1)^k, not from svd null bases N_r, N_l as the oracle does:
//     two converged 144 x 144 Jacobi svds (20 sweeps; 10 leave five null sigmas unconverged)
//     overrun the interpreter lane's 1e9-step budget (BL8005), as do two on the 78 symmetric forms.
//     Basis-free evidence: tr R = sum_L mult_L delta / (delta - L(L+1)) = 10147632/3792343 at
//     delta = 1/10, and tr P0 = 6.
// (ii) R = M^(1/2) by eigh; L_a = R J~_a R^-1 is antisymmetric.
// (iii) J_a = R F_a R^-1, negated if c_12^3 < 0: [J_x, J_y] = J_z cyclically and kappa = -2 I.
// (iv) The Casimir sum_a J_a^2 is -l(l+1) on each isotypic block: 0 x1, -2 x6, -6 x5.
// (v) Per l, the intertwiners T J_a = D_a^(l) T: the stacked (I (x) J_a^T - D_a (x) I) vec T
//     (row-major vec) has singular values sqrt(L(L+1)) over the total spins L of D_l (x) V,
//     so its nullity is the multiplicity of L = 0 -- n_l = 1, 2, 1, Schur made visible. The
//     null vectors are Loewdin-orthonormalized, scaled by sqrt(2l+1) and stacked into U.
// Basis-free quantities are pinned entry by entry: the vec-stack sigmas, Killing eigenvalues,
// M and its spectrum, R and the Casimir matrix against the oracle; tr R, the Casimir spectrum
// and the intertwiner ladders against their closed forms. U itself is
// fixed only up to a sign per n_l = 1 block and O(2) on the l = 1 pair, so it is pinned
// through U U^T = I and the final residual max_a |U J_a U^T - D_a| <= 1e-10.
// Spelling notes. F's Casimir is summed with lie.mm: lie.casimir returns (sum_a L_a^2)^T,
// the same only for antisymmetric L (as in step iv). Omega and the intertwiner systems are
// built inside functions (keeping the 144 x 144 operands out of the output) that take their
// arrays as PARAMETERS: a function called from inside another function cannot read module
// bindings (g++ "not declared"). m.solve inside a kernel must be let-bound (BL7001 otherwise).
import math as m
import lie
type D = Idx<12>
type G = Idx<3>
type V2 = Idx<144>
type K2 = Idx<2>
type H0 = Idx<36>
type H1r = Idx<108>
type H1c = Idx<36>
type H2r = Idx<180>
type H2c = Idx<60>
